.\"##
.\"
.\" Manual page of "mcp-python-container" - the launcher of the MCP server
.\" "mcp-python" in a Docker container, for the current user. The secrets,
.\" the environment and the security are described here for
.\" "mcp-python-compose" too.
.\"
.\" View the source: man ./container/mcp-python-container.1
.TH MCP-PYTHON-CONTAINER 1 2026-11-15 "mcp-python-container" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mcp-python-container \- the MCP server mcp-python of the current user, in a Docker container
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mcp-python-container
.RI [ "docker run options" ]
.br
.B mcp-python-container secrets
.br
.B mcp-python-container
.RB { \-h | \-\-help }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mcp-python-container
starts the
.BR mcp-python (8)
server - an MCP server, which runs a Python 3 code for its clients - in a
container of the local Docker, as a service of the user who runs it, with
.BR "docker run" :
in the foreground, until Ctrl C. No image registry is needed and no Python
at the host. The same server in the background -
.BR mcp-python-compose (1).
.PP
HTTP at port
.B 8765
and HTTPS at port
.BR 8766 ,
published at
.B 127.0.0.1
of the host
.RB ( MCP_PUBLISH_HOST ).
The arguments are more options of
.BR "docker run" ,
e.g.
.BR "\-\-env MCP_EXEC_TIMEOUT=120" .
.PP
At each start, before the container, the launcher (and
.BR mcp-python-compose (1)
too):
.IP \(bu 2
makes the secrets, which are absent - only those (see FILES);
.IP \(bu 2
sets their access modes - readable by the user only;
.IP \(bu 2
loads the image from the archive of the package, if the local Docker has
no image of the version of the package;
.IP \(bu 2
prints a
.B curl
command per listener, to check it.
.PP
.B mcp-python-container secrets
does the first two only, with no container and no Docker, and prints the
paths as the settings of the server
.RB ( MCP_TLS_CERT ,
.BR MCP_TLS_KEY ,
.BR MCP_AUTH_TOKENS )
and the token of the client
.RB ( MCP_CLIENT_TOKEN ).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/mcp-python/
The secrets of the user
.RB ( MCP_DATA_DIR ).
The directories - mode 0700.
.TP
.I tls/tls.key\fR, \fPtls/tls.crt
The key (mode 0600) and the self-signed certificate of the HTTPS listener,
for
.BR localhost ,
.B 127.0.0.1
and the full and the short name of the host. A client has to trust the
certificate - see
.BR mcp-python (8),
HTTPS WITH A SELF-SIGNED CERTIFICATE; the launchers do not do it.
.TP
.I tokens/<client>
The SHA-256 of the token of a client, mode 0600 - the file the server
reads.
.TP
.I clients/<client>.token
The token itself, mode 0600 - for the client, in the header
.BR "Authorization: Bearer <token>" .
.TP
.I /usr/lib/mcp-python-container/mcp-python_<version>_container.run
The image as a self-extracting archive - see its
.BR \-\-help .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CONTAINER_TOOL
.B docker
(default) or
.BR podman .
.TP
.B MCP_CLIENT
The client to make a token for, if absent. Default - the user name.
.TP
.B MCP_DATA_DIR
The directory of the secrets. Default
.IR ${XDG_DATA_HOME:\-~/.local/share}/mcp-python .
.TP
.B MCP_IMAGE_TAG
The tag of the image
.BR mcp-python .
Default - the version of the package.
.TP
.B MCP_PUBLISH_HOST
The host address of the listeners. Default
.BR 127.0.0.1 .
.TP
.B MCP_CPUS
The CPUs limit of the container, as a number of CPUs. Default - 75% of the
CPUs of the host.
.SH SECURITY
The container starts as root with three capabilities only
.RB ( SETUID ,
.BR SETGID ,
.BR DAC_READ_SEARCH ).
The server reads the key and the token files - files of the user, mode
0600 - then drops to its own account in the container, and the
capabilities are gone. A submitted code runs as that account and can not
read the secrets. The rest - a read only file system, the scratch is the
only writable place, memory, processes and CPUs limits - as the Systemd
unit of
.BR mcp-python (8)
has.
.PP
The token files are read once, at the start
.RB ( MCP_AUTH_RELOAD_PERIOD=once ).
A client added or removed - a restart of the server.
.PP
The certificate is not renewed. Expired - a warning at the start; a new
one - delete
.I tls
and start again.
.SH EXAMPLES
The server, until Ctrl C:
.PP
.RS
.EX
mcp-python-container
.EE
.RE
.PP
One more client - its token in
.IR clients/laptop.token ,
at the next start:
.PP
.RS
.EX
MCP_CLIENT=laptop mcp-python-container
.EE
.RE
.PP
A client removed - then a restart:
.PP
.RS
.EX
rm ~/.local/share/mcp-python/tokens/laptop \e
   ~/.local/share/mcp-python/clients/laptop.token
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mcp-python-compose (1),
.BR mcp-python (8),
.BR mcp-python-token (8),
.BR docker-run (1),
.BR curl (1)
